    "finalText": "Done. The implementation is complete and verified:\n\n- **`main.go`** — `migrate`/`serve` subcommands, chi router (chi v5.2.1), server on `0.0.0.0:8000`, `DATABASE_URL` read from env via `database/sql` + pgx\n- **`handlers.go`** — all five endpoints with validation: 201 create (generated or custom code), 409 duplicate, 404 unknown code, 302 redirect with atomic single-click increment (`UPDATE ... RETURNING`), ordered list with `total`, 422 for malformed JSON/invalid url/code\n- **`migrate.go` + `migrations/`** — embedded, idempotent SQL migrations tracked in `schema_migrations`\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — builds, applies pending migrations, serves in the foreground; deps vendored so no installs at startup\n- **`README.md`** — documents `sh start.sh` startup\n\nTested end-to-end: 19 API checks plus edge cases (trailing garbage, null code, non-string url, invalid path codes), restart persistence (clicks survived), and a clean cold start — test data truncated, port 8000 free for the harness."
